WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.750
An ancient Hindu hymn
says that truth is one,

2
00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:06.540
and the wise call it by many names.

3
00:00:06.590 --> 00:00:10.730
Inside Hinduism itself, many
traditions live side by side,

4
00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:13.360
with no single creed or authority.

5
00:00:13.410 --> 00:00:17.820
And in Britain, many mandirs open their
doors to school visits and interfaith

6
00:00:17.870 --> 00:00:18.890
events.

7
00:00:18.940 --> 00:00:22.030
So can a Hindu believe
every path reaches God,

8
00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:24.940
and still think one path is best?

9
00:00:24.990 --> 00:00:28.380
In this mission, you'll map
four views of other religions,

10
00:00:28.430 --> 00:00:30.940
from exclusivism to pluralism.

11
00:00:30.990 --> 00:00:35.370
Then you'll test verses from the Gita,
and see how Hindus live alongside other

12
00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:37.820
faiths, from India to Britain.

13
00:00:37.870 --> 00:00:42.850
Your mission: weigh up how Hindus can
honour other paths and still hold to their

14
00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:43.310
own.
